Modifications made to the upstream source
-----------------------------------------
The following changes are carried on top of upstream commit fada664
(AGPL-3.0 §5 requires this notice; §13 requires that users who interact
with this program over a network be offered the Corresponding Source,
which the link above provides):

1. Product identity renamed from "RustDesk" to "NEILICO"
   (application name, GTK/Android/macOS/Windows bundle identifiers,
   window titles, desktop entries, systemd unit, package descriptions).

2. Default rendezvous (ID) and relay server, and the default server
   public key, changed from the official RustDesk servers to our own
   self-hosted hbbs/hbbr deployment. See libs/hbb_common/src/config.rs
   (NEILICO_ID_SERVER / RENDEZVOUS_SERVERS / RS_PUB_KEY). These are
   overridable at build time via the NEILICO_ID_SERVER and
   NEILICO_PUB_KEY environment variables.

3. Application icons replaced with NEILICO artwork.

4. The in-client "About" page adds a link to the NEILICO Corresponding
   Source and a modification notice; the upstream copyright line is
   retained.

No upstream copyright, license text, or attribution has been removed.

